# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What is versioned here, and what is not.
#
# The repository is the SOURCE of three things — the agent preset, the engine it
# drives, and the two documents that explain both — plus a small curated set of
# examples. Everything else is either a dependency, a build artifact, or the
# harness's own directory. See REPO-LAYOUT.md for the full map.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── bulk material that only THIS machine needs ───────────────────────────────
# `engine/assets/` (17 files, 5.9 MB) and `engine/refs/` (3 files, 3.5 MB) are INPUT
# material for scenes authored on this machine — game character art, processed
# cut-outs, reference posters. They are not part of the toolchain: a fresh clone is
# meant to make its OWN work, not to rebuild this machine's posters.
#
# Consequence, stated plainly so nobody is surprised: the scenes under
# `engine/scenes/` reference these files by ABSOLUTE path, so a fresh clone cannot
# render them, and `examples/` cannot be regenerated from source. The engine, the 25
# session tools, the preset and all 13 test suites work without them — that is the
# line that was drawn, and the test suites were made self-contained to hold it.
#
# Untracked means untracked, not deleted: this machine keeps its copies on disk.
engine/assets/
engine/refs/

# ── dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reproduce with `npm install` in engine/. @napi-rs/canvas ships per-platform
# native binaries (a 27 MB skia build), so a committed copy is both large and
# wrong on any machine that is not this one.
engine/node_modules/
node_modules/

# ── build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# engine/out/ holds 42 files and about 46 MB of renders, measurement reports and
# PSDs that are rewritten on every iteration. They regenerate in about a second
# each from the scenes committed beside them, which is the definition of
# something that does not belong in a commit.
#
# The curated subset that IS versioned lives in examples/ — excluded from the
# rule below on purpose, because a design engine with no picture in its
# repository has to be taken on faith. `node make-examples.mjs` promotes them.
engine/out/
!examples/

# Photoshop bridge logs, written into the engine directory by jsx/psx.ps1.
engine/.probe/
.probe/

# ── the scratch cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything that is regenerated on demand now lives in ONE place, and that place is
# OUTSIDE the repository: `../.cache/` beside it. See .cache/README.md.
#
#   ../.cache/video/           decoded video frames, ffmpeg temp, alpha fixtures
#   ../.cache/test/            what the test suites write (scope renders, selftest)
#   ../.cache/render-scratch/  one-off probe and iteration renders
#
# The reason is maintenance, not repository size. A cache that sits inside the tree —
# even gitignored — still gets backed up, copied and, worst of all, mistaken for a
# deliverable. `engine/out/` now holds NOTHING but real render artifacts, which is what
# makes "is this a finished poster or leftover probe output?" answerable at a glance.
#
# Measured: one 20-second clip decode produced 948 frames and 1.06 GB. A first staging
# pass once swept all of it into a commit.
.cache/
engine/.vp-frames/
engine/.vp-tmp/

# ── editor and scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No leading slash and no trailing slash: `engine/scenes/.idea/` is nested, and a
# `.idea/` pattern anchored at the root missed it. The JetBrains directory was
# sitting in the tree untracked-but-unignored until this was fixed.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.bak
*.tmp
*.log

# ── the harness home ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `design/` above is the canonical preset source. `node deploy-preset.mjs`
# INSTALLS it into %USERPROFILE%\.dsh\.agent-presets\design — that directory is a
# deploy target, and nothing under the harness home is versioned here. The two
# are kept in step by running the script, never by editing both.
